      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Lock the go-to-market launch plan, channels and budget allocation.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Alright team, let's discuss the go-to-market strategy. I've drafted the 'Go-to-Market Launch Plan' (A3) and the initial 'Launch Budget and Spend Tracker' (A2). Please review and share your feedback on the channel mix, timeline, and budget split for T3. CC @320085 @514149 @270220 @59927",
            "mentions": [
              320085,
              514149,
              270220,
              59927
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "A2",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 320085,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks. Looking at A2, I see a significant portion of the budget is allocated to paid social. Can you walk me through the thinking there versus leveraging our existing email list more heavily?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 270220,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "The timeline in A3 looks tight but achievable. For T5, when do we need the final creative brief approved to hit the asset production deadlines?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "The primary objective is new customer acquisition, so the budget is weighted towards top-of-funnel channels like paid social. However, you're right, we shouldn't neglect our warm audience. We can reallocate some funds to a more robust email campaign.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Good question. The creative brief for T5 needs to be locked by this Friday to give the design team enough time.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 59927,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Is the total budget in A2 final? What if we need more for a specific channel?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 514149,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "The channel mix seems reasonable, focusing on acquisition. The timeline aligns with the 21-day constraint. No major concerns from my side.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "@59927 Yes, the total budget is fixed as per the project constraints. Any changes must be reallocations between channels, not an increase in the total.",
            "mentions": [
              59927
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 320085,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I suggest we move 15% of the paid social budget to fund a dedicated 3-part email nurture campaign. That should give us a good balance.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "I like that suggestion. It's a smart adjustment. Let's proceed with that change. With this, I think we can approve the final channel mix and launch timeline.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 2
              }
