      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Finalize customer journey, operational processes and readiness checklist.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 514149,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, I've drafted the 'Customer Journey and Experience Blueprint' (A4) and the 'Operational Playbook' (A7). These cover the initial work for T4 and T8. Would appreciate your review, especially on the key touchpoints and the billing/support processes. @242297 @320085 @59927 @270220",
            "mentions": [
              242297,
              320085,
              59927,
              270220
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "A7",
              "T4",
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "The journey map in A4 is very clear, nice work. One question: I don't see a specific quality control checkpoint just before the first renewal charge. We should add one to ensure the customer experience is smooth heading into the second month.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 320085,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "This is a solid start. I noticed in A7, the cancellation flow is purely transactional. We should consider adding a 'save offer' step. It's a standard retention tactic and could significantly reduce voluntary churn.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 59927,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "If a customer's payment fails, who sends them an email? Is that a support task in the playbook?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 514149,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "@59927 That's an automated notification from our billing system. The process is documented in A7 under 'Dunning and Failed Payments'. Support only gets involved if the customer replies with an issue.",
            "mentions": [
              59927
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 514149,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Great feedback. I'll add the pre-renewal quality checkpoint to A4 and the 'save offer' step to the cancellation flow in A7. Thanks @242297 and @320085.",
            "mentions": [
              242297,
              320085
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Perfect. With those additions, I'm happy to approve the customer journey and its checkpoints.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 320085,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Now that the journey is set, we should create the 'Pre-Launch Readiness and Quality Checklist' (A5) for our go/no-go review (T10). It should be based on the key steps in A4 and A7.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T10",
              "A4",
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Agreed. @320085, can you take the first pass at drafting the checklist in A5?",
            "mentions": [
              320085
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 320085,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Will do. I've just put together the initial draft in A5. It covers marketing, ops, and support readiness. Please take a look.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 270220,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "The checklist in A5 looks thorough. Covers all the critical points for my area.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 242297,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "This is exactly what we need for the T10 review. I approve this pre-launch readiness checklist.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
